Check if there are any two Equal numbers in an array at a distance less than or equal to k

Explanation:
Iterate throught the array till the point of i and check if there ar eany occurance of the equal number in the hashmap till then, 
if so retireve the index, else put the num and its index on the map


Code:
class Solution {
    public boolean containsNearbyDuplicate(int[] nums, int k) {
        int n=nums.length;
        HashMap<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        boolean ans=false;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            int num=nums[i];

            if(map.containsKey(num)){
                if(Math.abs(i-map.get(num)) <=k ){
                    ans=true;
                }
            }

            map.put(num,i);
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
